From 7e5f0e7c3151b04b66cc4192040685f581a89897 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sjcsf <346224915+llsf2020@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] FreeChat: strict mode and global privacy settings on iOS

Strict mode (per device, opt-in): sign-ins use the SDK's in-memory store and are
never saved to the keychain, the app signs out on return after the chosen time
in the background, and password sign-ins use a device ID the homeserver removes
once idle. Settings gain my default burn-after-read, protection for every chat
and the strict mode switch. Untested: needs a Mac to build.
